<<feedback: a bug that comes and goes>>=
"feedback": {"neutral": "<p>A failure that cannot be made to happen on demand cannot be studied: reading the crash, locating the fault and checking a fix all need a run you can repeat, so the first move is to find what the crashing runs have in common. Wrapping the program in try and except hides the crash instead of explaining it; leaving it assumes that a failure which is rare is harmless; and retyping the program assumes the fault is in the typing rather than in what the program does.</p>"}
@

Reading the crash report: each distractor is a way of not reading
it---as a missing file, as Python failing to read the code, or as
ordinary output.

