The main function ties the pieces together: fetch (or read) the
report, keep the consenting students' rows, tabulate and summarise,
and---for the background quiz, whose open items are the ones that get
coded---pre-code if asked to and write the sheet.
The background report carries the consent item, so its own rows
answer who consented; for the debugging quizzes the set comes from
the background report, fetched by default or read from a saved copy
with [[--consent-from]].
The option is not mere convenience: a saved report has no login
column, so its rows key by course and name
(\cref{app:student-identity}), and a consent set keyed by fetched
login IDs would match none of them---the two reports have to come the
same way for the join to be a join.
If every row is filtered away, the program says so and stops, since
each summary below would otherwise report an empty cohort as if it
were a finding.
A saved report is read by the same reader as a fetched one
(\cref{app:reading-the-report}) and in the encoding Canvas wrote it
in, byte-order mark and all, so the two paths differ in where the
bytes come from and in nothing else.

<<analysis main>>=
def read_rows(path, titles):
    """Read a saved student-analysis report, keyed by item title."""
    with open(path, encoding="utf-8-sig", newline="") as infile:
        return read_report(infile.read(), titles)


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
    parser.add_argument("--quiz", choices=QUIZ_TITLES, default="background",
                        help="which quiz to analyse")
    parser.add_argument("--results",
                        help="read this CSV instead of fetching from Canvas")
    parser.add_argument("--consent-from",
                        help="saved background report to read the consent"
                             " set from (default: fetch the background quiz)")
    parser.add_argument("--llm", action="store_true",
                        help="pre-code the open answers with an LLM")
    parser.add_argument("--coding-sheet", default="quiz-coding-sheet.csv",
                        help="output CSV for the coding of open answers")
    args = parser.parse_args()

    titles = titles_of(args.quiz)
    if args.results:
        rows = read_rows(args.results, titles)
    else:
        rows = fetch_results(args.quiz, titles)
    if not rows:
        sys.exit("no responses")

    students = consenting(rows)
    if students is None:
        <<derive the consent set from the background report>>
    rows = filter_consent(rows, students)
    if not rows:
        sys.exit("no consenting students")

    print(f"{len(rows)} students")
    for item in CLOSED_ITEMS:
        tabulate(rows, item)
    summarize_scores(rows)
    if args.quiz == "background":
        suggestions = llm_precode(rows) if args.llm else None
        write_coding_sheet(rows, args.coding_sheet, suggestions)
        print(f"\ncoding sheet written to {args.coding_sheet}")
