\paragraph{Reading an export}

The export is a CSV in the loosest sense, and four of its habits have
to be met before any of it can be read.
It is UTF-8 with a byte order mark, so it is opened as [[utf-8-sig]]
rather than [[utf-8]], which would otherwise hand us a first column
name with an invisible character glued to its front.
It is semicolon-delimited, as Swedish spreadsheet exports are.
It opens with a preamble---the source, the report's name, the läsår, and
blank lines---whose length is not the same in the two exports we read:
the grundskola header sits on line six and the gymnasium header on line
seven.
So the header is found rather than counted, by looking for the line
that has the huvudman column among its fields, which is a property of
the header rather than of any particular report's layout.
And it ends with a trailer of prose---the report's description and
definitions---which parses as rows with almost every field empty.

We could not tell that trailer from a school by its name field, which
is where the prose lands, but every real row carries a school unit
code and no prose line does.
That also disposes of the register's suppressed cells, written as a
lone [[.]] where a figure is withheld for privacy: the identifying
columns are never suppressed, so a row whose unit code is a [[.]] or
empty is not a school.

<<read one register export>>=
NAME_COLUMN = "Skola"
UNIT_COLUMN = "Skol-enhetskod"
KOMMUN_COLUMN = "Skolkommun"
HUVUDMAN_COLUMN = "Typ av huvudman"
SUPPRESSED = "."


def read_export(path):
    """Return the school-unit rows of one mirrored SIRIS export."""
    with open(path, encoding="utf-8-sig", newline="") as export:
        return parse_export(export.read().splitlines())


def parse_export(lines):
    """Return the school-unit rows among the lines of an export."""
    header = None
    for number, line in enumerate(lines):
        if HUVUDMAN_COLUMN in line.split(";"):
            header = number
            break
    if header is None:
        raise ValueError(f"no header row naming {HUVUDMAN_COLUMN!r}")
    rows = csv.DictReader(lines[header:], delimiter=";")
    return [row for row in rows if cell(row, UNIT_COLUMN)]


def cell(row, column):
    """Return one register cell, reading a suppressed cell as empty."""
    value = (row.get(column) or "").strip()
    return "" if value == SUPPRESSED else value
@

