\paragraph{The register's vocabulary and ours}

The register does not write its huvudman types the way we want to code
them, and it has not written them the same way throughout: the
gymnasium exports say \enquote{Landsting} up to läsår 2018/19 and
\enquote{Region} from 2019/20, for the same twelve schools, because the
landsting were renamed regions in 2020 and the register followed.
A study that read the labels literally would find a school type
appearing and another vanishing in the middle of its data, so the
labels are mapped onto our tokens deliberately, and the old name and
the new both land on [[region]].

The table also holds tokens the two mirrored exports never produce.
[[statlig]] belongs to specialskolan and sameskolan, which are separate
school forms with their own exports; [[utlandsskola]] belongs to the
Swedish schools abroad, which the register carries under a placeholder
huvudman; and [[abroad]] is for schooling that was never Swedish.
Those three are the coder's to apply, and they are listed here because
the sheet's vocabulary is one vocabulary whether the register or the
coder wrote the value.
Komvux belongs in the same list: a municipality is the huvudman of its
komvux by law even when the teaching is contracted out to Hermods or
NTI (skollagen 23 kap.\ 2 §), so a komvux answer is [[kommunal]]
regardless of whose name is over the door---and no lookup would find
it, since komvux units are in neither export.

<<the register's vocabulary and ours>>=
UNKNOWN = "unknown"
ABROAD = "abroad"
HUVUDMAN_TOKENS = {
    "kommunal": "kommunal",
    "enskild": "enskild",
    "region": "region",
    "landsting": "region",
    "statlig": "statlig",
    "stat": "statlig",
}


def huvudman_token(value):
    """Return the study's token for a register huvudman type."""
    return HUVUDMAN_TOKENS.get(normalize(value), UNKNOWN)
@

